<br/>
<br/>Most top-end pre-raid setups revolve around hitting the 2005 Haste breakpoint. This becomes easily reachable in Phase 3 with a healthy mix of 359s and some 378 gear; if you're, however, struggling to reach that point, you should opt for the 916 Haste breakpoint instead. <br/>
<br/>Due to reforging, most items are - outside of Haste when reaching breakpoints - functionally equivalent to each other as long as they're the same item level. Intellect itself remains extremely powerful compared to any secondary stat, meaning that differences between same-ilvl gear are small.<br/>
<br/>Overall, this means that for our gearing strategy, there isn't necessarily a single "best option" per item level if multiple items at the same ilvl exist. This excludes trinkets, which have an entirely separate grading scale that you should consult the table for.<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="justice-points">Justice Points for Restoration Druid Healer Pre-Raid</h3>
<a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/currency=395/justice-points">
<span>
<img alt="Justice Points" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/pvecurrency-justice.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Justice Points</span></span></a> are one of the two new PvE currencies in Cataclysm (<a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/currency=396/valor-points">
<span>
<img alt="Valor Points" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/pvecurrency-valor.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Valor Points</span></span></a> being the other one). They have a hard cap of 4,000 and can never go over it, but unlike the <a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/currency=396/valor-points">
<span>
<img alt="Valor Points" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/pvecurrency-valor.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Valor Points</span></span></a>, there is no weekly limit on how much you can earn. In theory, dedicated players can go from 0 to 4,000 in a single day. It is worth noting that whenever a new raid phase is released, all of the <a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/currency=396/valor-points">
<span>
<img alt="Valor Points" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/pvecurrency-valor.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Valor Points</span></span></a> a player has get converted into JPs, but never over the cap. Additionally, previous Valor gear will be converted to costing <a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/currency=395/justice-points">
<span>
<img alt="Justice Points" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/pvecurrency-justice.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Justice Points</span></span></a> instead and new sets of <a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/currency=396/valor-points">
<span>
<img alt="Valor Points" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/pvecurrency-valor.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Valor Points</span></span></a> gear will be added.<br/>
<br/>In effect, Justice Points are the "catchup mechanism" for new 85s, being used to purchase catch-up pre-raid gear. In Phase 3, all Justice Point gear is ilvl 359. It's is a good way to shore up any slots between crafted BoEs and where you've been unlucky from dungeon drops.<br/>
<br/>All of these options are listed in no particular order, and are not individually priority to purchase. If you don't have a 346 item in a particular slot and the Justice Point vendor sells an item for that slot, you should buy it.<br/>
<br/>
