<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="valor-points">Valor Points for Restoration Druid Healer Pre-Raid</h3>
<a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/currency=396/valor-points">
<span>
<img alt="Valor Points" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/pvecurrency-valor.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Valor Points</span></span></a> are a type of currency that is rewarded via participating in instanced PvE content, such as dungeons and raids, and is used to purchase comparable gear to normal-mode raid drops (ilvl 378 in Phase 3). It's also used to directly purchase tier gloves, chest, and legs, which MUST be purchased - there is no way to obtain these items otherwise, except through getting very lucky in <a data-entity="zone" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/zone=5600/baradin-hold">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Baradin Hold</span></a>.<br/>
<br/>
<a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/currency=396/valor-points">
<span>
<img alt="Valor Points" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/pvecurrency-valor.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Valor Points</span></span></a> are the higher of the two tiers of PvE currency, and are rewarded for completing the random heroic dungeons and defeating raid bosses. However, unlike <a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/currency=395/justice-points">
<span>
<img alt="Justice Points" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/pvecurrency-justice.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Justice Points</span></span></a>, Valor is capped at a rolling seasonal cap rate of 1600, so purchases must be carefully planned out. Therefore, the following table is a generalized recommendation of the order in which you should purchase Valor items.<br/>
<br/>However, here are some following caveats. Firstly, ilvl is king - but not in the way you might think. <b>Since 391 tier requires the 378 tier item to upgrade, you MUST spend <a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/currency=396/valor-points">
<span>
<img alt="Valor Points" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/pvecurrency-valor.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Valor Points</span></span></a> on gloves/<wbr/>chest/<wbr/>legs as mentioned previously if you have the respective heroic token - so this takes absolute priority over all else, as Valor gear is otherwise only 378.</b> Secondly, points are not exactly commensurate with the stat budget gain - that is to say, chest and legs are generally more "bang for your buck" than gloves, which are more efficient than ring or relic, which are more efficient than relics. In essence this means the bigger Valor purchases are more impactful are the pieces on their own. <br/>
<br/>
