<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="trinkets-for-restoration-druid-healer">Trinkets for Restoration Druid Healer</h4>In P3, available pre-raid trinkets are in a spot where the gap between the 1st and 2nd is very large. The single best option available is <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=65124/fall-of-mortality">
<img alt="Fall of Mortality" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_cat_trinket12.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Fall of Mortality</span></a> while either <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=70142/moonwell-chalice">
<img alt="Moonwell Chalice" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_potion_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Moonwell Chalice</span></a>, <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=62050/darkmoon-card-tsunami">
<img alt="Darkmoon Card: Tsunami" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_inscription_tarot_tsunamicard.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Darkmoon Card: Tsunami</span></a> or <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=64645/tyrandes-favorite-doll">
<img alt="Tyrande's Favorite Doll" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_archaeology_tyrandesfavoritedoll.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Tyrande's Favorite Doll</span></a> are fine to use as 2nd trinket in this context. <br/>
<br/>
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=60233/shard-of-woe">
<img alt="Shard of Woe" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_frost_iceshard.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Shard of Woe</span></a> may seem tempting but with how Druid and Haste works, it's use is very niche and situational. If you opt to go with it, you have to <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/guide/classes/druid/restoration/healer-stat-priority-attributes-pve">reforge to 2032 Haste instead of 2005 so you reach the next breakpoint</a> for an extra tick of <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=774/rejuvenation">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_nature_rejuvenation.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Rejuvenation</span></a>, <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=48438/wild-growth">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_druid_flourish.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Wild Growth</span></a> and <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=81275/efflorescence">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_herb_talandrasrose.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Efflorescence</span></a> when <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=60233/shard-of-woe">
<img alt="Shard of Woe" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_frost_iceshard.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Shard of Woe</span></a> one-use is activated.   <br/>
<br/>As for <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=68777/vibrant-alchemist-stone">
<img alt="Vibrant Alchemist Stone" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/item_alchemiststonec.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Vibrant Alchemist Stone</span></a>, the overall MP5 gained from this trinket varies depending on the fight length, making it strong if your boss kills are are quick, however, the longer the fight, the worse the this trinket becomes for MP5.<div class="pad"></div>
