<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="main-hand-weapons-for-restoration-druid-healer">Main Hand Weapons for Restoration Druid Healer</h4>
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=70157/lightforged-elementium-hammer">
<img alt="Lightforged Elementium Hammer" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_mace_84.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Lightforged Elementium Hammer</span></a> paired with the <a data-entity="zone" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/zone=5733/molten-front">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Molten Front</span></a> off hand is the best pre-raid combination for Phase 3. However, since this requires once again another big gold and time investment, it's worth noting that the next best main hand options come from <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/guide/dungeons/elemental-rune-protocol-inferno-dungeons-overview">Elemental Rune Dungeons</a>. If you don't have either <span class="q4">Epic Staff</span> from <a class="icontiny" data-entity="skill" data-game="wow" data-type="skill" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/skill=794/archaeology">
<img alt="Archaeology" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_archaeology.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Archaeology</span></a>, the difference in between these options is rather marginal.<br/>
<br/>
